      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1792757623458,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Check whether the tree is empty or not .\n\n2. If tree is empty print \"tree is empty \" and return .\n\n3. If tree is not empty do the following :\n\n4. start pointer from root node and move towards left node pushing each node\nin stack .\n\n5. Stop when u pointer becomes null .\n\n6. Check whether the stack is empty or not .\n\n7. If stack is empty then stop .\n\n8. If it is not empty then :\n\n a. pop the top node from stack .\n\n b. print it \n\n c. check whether it has right child or not .\n\n d. if it has right child move the pointer to right and go to step 4 .\n\n e. If it does not has a RIGHT child then goto step 6.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. Check whether the tree is empty or not .\n\n2. If tree is empty print \"tree is empty \" and return .\n\n3. If tree is not empty do the following :\n\n4. start pointer from root node and move towards left node pushing each node in stack .\n\n5. Stop when u pointer becomes null .\n\n6. Check whether the stack is empty or not .\n\n7. If stack is empty then stop .\n\n8. If it is not empty then :\n\n a. pop the top node from stack .\n\n b. print it \n\n c. check whether it has right child or not .\n\n d. if it has right child move the pointer to right and go to step 4 .\n\n e. If it does not has a RIGHT child then goto step 6.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
